    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/spencerjamesstewart/anki-template-engine/commit/c3e90635d8f5b958240b5ca6e739eea6be02513e"/>
    <title>
        feat: add input/ folder with auto-archive on successful gen
    </title>
    <updated>2026-07-22T05:43:17Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289839794?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>spencerjamesstewart</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/spencerjamesstewart</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: add input/ folder with auto-archive on successful gen

Drivers declare source files via new register_input(), which prints an
&amp;#39;Input: &amp;lt;abspath&amp;gt;&amp;#39; contract line. After a fully successful gen run,
run.sh moves consumed inputs to input/archive/&amp;lt;batch&amp;gt;/ so the same
source can&amp;#39;t be regenerated by accident. Docs rewritten to the
repo-as-workspace model; gen_medterm.py repointed to input/.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
