    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/spencerjamesstewart/anki-template-engine/commit/a9c728f16208c5f9835ae972b155985a4ff91801"/>
    <title>
        feat!: add tags column and subject-neutralize engine
    </title>
    <updated>2026-07-14T03:00:07Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289839794?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>spencerjamesstewart</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/spencerjamesstewart</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat!: add tags column and subject-neutralize engine

Deck output gains a third tags column (#tags column:3); build_deck
takes deck-wide tags, merges per-card tags, and raises on untagged
cards or tags with whitespace. Rename clinical -&amp;gt; in_context
(chart -&amp;gt; excerpt) and drug_name -&amp;gt; alias. Rebuild sample deck as
mixed-domain, non-medical. Rewrite INSTRUCTIONS.md around Anki as
cold-recall layer: drop Type II/III question blocks, add Tags
section, bound true/false trap cards.

BREAKING CHANGE: card types clinical and drug_name removed;
validate_deck now requires three columns and tags&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
